448eb8f9431c950eec2c19465e0330df947b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commits/b3e448eb8f9431c950eec2c19465e0330df947b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commits/aeef02a1c0f08a79468977523c29e24f95da5ee2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-08T16:52:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-08T16:52:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix auth, memory management, and implement dynamic style-mimicry\n\nAuthentication:\n- Create lib/server/anthropic.js: shared server-side singleton with\n  explicit process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY validation at init time\n- Clear error message when key is missing instead of opaque SDK error\n- Both API routes now use getAnthropicClient() instead of bare\n  `new Anthropic()` which relied on implicit env var detection\n- Auth errors surfaced to client with proper 500 status\n\nMemory management (clientParser.js):\n- Nullify originalBuffer immediately after creating slice(0) copies\n- Nullify pdfBuffer after pdfjs-dist detaches it via getDocument()\n- Nullify scanBuffer/scanArray after JPEG binary scan completes\n- Nullify zipBuffer after JSZip extraction in finally block\n- Nullify mammothBuffer after convertToHtml, create fresh textCopy\n  for extractRawText, then nullify textCopy after use\n- Nullify arrayBuffer in parseDocumentClientSide via try/finally\n- All buffer lifecycle: create copy → use → nullify → GC eligible\n\nDynamic style-mimicry:\n- /api/extract-style now accepts dual inputs: referenceTexts[] and\n  targetMedicalData (sample of the document to be restyled)\n- LLM prompt instructs: (a) analyze references for consistent style,\n  structural layout, and tone; (b) calibrate for the target document''s\n  medical domain; (c) maintain medical accuracy and professional\n  veterinary terminology\n- DocumentUpload sends first 2000 chars of parsed text as target context\n\nStreaming support:\n- /api/restyle-chunk supports ?stream=true query param for SSE streaming\n- Uses client.messages.stream() with ReadableStream for long chunks\n- Stays within Vercel timeout by streaming tokens incrementally\n\nModel: claude-opus-4-20250514 (highest reasoning, medical accuracy)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01VangytH8DhEu4NDFFJeduF","tree":{"sha":"8a010bf7f48f22fa08b81a2dc2205ce219f1467b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/git/trees/8a010bf7f48f22fa08b81a2dc2205ce219f1467b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/git/commits/aeef02a1c0f08a79468977523c29e24f95da5ee2","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a010bf7f48f22fa08b81a2dc2205ce219f1467b\nparent 8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1772988747 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1772988747 +0000\n\nFix auth, memory management, and implement dynamic style-mimicry\n\nAuthentication:\n- Create lib/server/anthropic.js: shared server-side singleton with\n  explicit process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY validation at init time\n- Clear error message when key is missing instead of opaque SDK error\n- Both API routes now use getAnthropicClient() instead of bare\n  `new Anthropic()` which relied on implicit env var detection\n- Auth errors surfaced to client with proper 500 status\n\nMemory management (clientParser.js):\n- Nullify originalBuffer immediately after creating slice(0) copies\n- Nullify pdfBuffer after pdfjs-dist detaches it via getDocument()\n- Nullify scanBuffer/scanArray after JPEG binary scan completes\n- Nullify zipBuffer after JSZip extraction in finally block\n- Nullify mammothBuffer after convertToHtml, create fresh textCopy\n  for extractRawText, then nullify textCopy after use\n- Nullify arrayBuffer in parseDocumentClientSide via try/finally\n- All buffer lifecycle: create copy → use → nullify → GC eligible\n\nDynamic style-mimicry:\n- /api/extract-style now accepts dual inputs: referenceTexts[] and\n  targetMedicalData (sample of the document to be restyled)\n- LLM prompt instructs: (a) analyze references for consistent style,\n  structural layout, and tone; (b) calibrate for the target document''s\n  medical domain; (c) maintain medical accuracy and professional\n  veterinary terminology\n- DocumentUpload sends first 2000 chars of parsed text as target context\n\nStreaming support:\n- /api/restyle-chunk supports ?stream=true query param for SSE streaming\n- Uses client.messages.stream() with ReadableStream for long chunks\n- Stays within Vercel timeout by streaming tokens incrementally\n\nModel: claude-opus-4-20250514 (highest reasoning, medical accuracy)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01VangytH8DhEu4NDFFJeduF\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJlX9hI9\ne0k62BCfzaLwQivpfVAi6QEPjENpHZ0ZoyOWsq9eXP+Nlz1Plq6y+4BkTuEf9kBsbIuV7t3fgleL\nOwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-08T16:52:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commit/aeef02a1c0f08a79468977523c29e24f95da5ee2","node_id":"C_kwDORhY08toAKGFlZWYwMmExYzBmMDhhNzk0Njg5Nzc1MjNjMjllMjRmOTVkYTVlZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commit/8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704","sha":"8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commits/8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704"}],"sha":"aeef02a1c0f08a79468977523c29e24f95da5ee2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commits/aeef02a1c0f08a79468977523c29e24f95da5ee2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commits/8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-08T14:25:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-08T14:25:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix detached ArrayBuffer crash; advanced image extraction pipeline\n\nRoot cause: pdfjs-dist transfers ownership of the ArrayBuffer passed\nvia { data: arrayBuffer }, detaching it. Subsequent code (binary JPEG\nscan, DOCX double-parse) then fails reading the same detached buffer.\n\nFix: Use arrayBuffer.slice(0) to create independent copies before\npassing to each consumer (pdfjs-dist, binary scanner, mammoth).\n\nImage extraction improvements:\n- PDF XObject extraction with CTM tracking for bounding box computation\n- Coordinate normalization from PDF space (bottom-left origin) to\n  browser convention (top-left origin)\n- SMask (soft mask) alpha compositing to prevent black-background\n  artifacts on transparent images\n- White background fill on all canvas renders for transparency safety\n- Vector graphic clustering: detect groups of consecutive path/stroke/\n  fill operations and render them as raster images via page.render()\n- Target DPI of 150 for web previews (2.08x scale from PDF''s 72 DPI)\n- Canvas cleanup (width=0, height=0) after each render to free memory\n- Image deduplication via quick hash to avoid XObject/binary-scan dupes\n\nDOCX improvements:\n- JSZip-based /word/media/ extraction for reliable image gallery\n- mammoth used for text extraction and as image fallback only\n- Buffer cloned separately for convertToHtml and extractRawText calls\n- UI note explaining that DOCX is reflowable (no page coords available)\n\nChunker: page-aware image distribution when pageNumber metadata exists\nImageInjector: data-page, data-bbox-*, data-source attributes on tags\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01VangytH8DhEu4NDFFJeduF","tree":{"sha":"9caeb5269317b68b99b611bdf928af37bedb88fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/git/trees/9caeb5269317b68b99b611bdf928af37bedb88fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/git/commits/8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704","verification":{"payload":"tree 9caeb5269317b68b99b611bdf928af37bedb88fa\nparent 1a8c926e2b40ab75fe8d97b03a6fad0ba5eaa6cf\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1772979929 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1772979929 +0000\n\nFix detached ArrayBuffer crash; advanced image extraction pipeline\n\nRoot cause: pdfjs-dist transfers ownership of the ArrayBuffer passed\nvia { data: arrayBuffer }, detaching it. Subsequent code (binary JPEG\nscan, DOCX double-parse) then fails reading the same detached buffer.\n\nFix: Use arrayBuffer.slice(0) to create independent copies before\npassing to each consumer (pdfjs-dist, binary scanner, mammoth).\n\nImage extraction improvements:\n- PDF XObject extraction with CTM tracking for bounding box computation\n- Coordinate normalization from PDF space (bottom-left origin) to\n  browser convention (top-left origin)\n- SMask (soft mask) alpha compositing to prevent black-background\n  artifacts on transparent images\n- White background fill on all canvas renders for transparency safety\n- Vector graphic clustering: detect groups of consecutive path/stroke/\n  fill operations and render them as raster images via page.render()\n- Target DPI of 150 for web previews (2.08x scale from PDF''s 72 DPI)\n- Canvas cleanup (width=0, height=0) after each render to free memory\n- Image deduplication via quick hash to avoid XObject/binary-scan dupes\n\nDOCX improvements:\n- JSZip-based /word/media/ extraction for reliable image gallery\n- mammoth used for text extraction and as image fallback only\n- Buffer cloned separately for convertToHtml and extractRawText calls\n- UI note explaining that DOCX is reflowable (no page coords available)\n\nChunker: page-aware image distribution when pageNumber metadata exists\nImageInjector: data-page, data-bbox-*, data-source attributes on tags\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01VangytH8DhEu4NDFFJeduF\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFfJ7T+k\nKrVaiPDH80KPRJHH4MTFurRfeVBUEg8DZjnAuA335Gay9JrcSWj/kQqp9M9/pUeQzpAzvEOLAy2h\nCwY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-08T14:25:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commit/8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704","node_id":"C_kwDORhY08toAKDhmOTJlYTA2MDcxM2I0N2QzMjlkOGM5NTQ2YmU0YmI2ZTA4OWU3MDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commit/1a8c926e2b40ab75fe8d97b03a6fad0ba5eaa6cf","sha":"1a8c926e2b40ab75fe8d97b03a6fad0ba5eaa6cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commits/1a8c926e2b40ab75fe8d97b03a6fad0ba5eaa6cf"}],"sha":"8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commits/8f92ea060713b47d329d8c9546be4bb6e089e704"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/commits/1a8c926e2b40ab75fe8d97b03a6fad0ba5eaa6cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-08T12:34:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-08T12:34:29Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Move document parsing to client-side, fix Vercel 4.5MB payload limit\n\nRoot cause: Uploading PDF/DOCX files as FormData to serverless functions\nhits Vercel''s 4.5MB body size limit, causing 413 errors.\n\nSolution: Parse documents entirely in the browser using pdfjs-dist (PDF)\nand mammoth (DOCX). No file binary ever hits the server — only small\nJSON text payloads are sent to the API routes.\n\nChanges:\n- Add lib/clientParser.js: browser-side PDF/DOCX text + image extraction\n  using pdfjs-dist and mammoth with canvas-based image rendering\n- Add lib/safeFetch.js: robust fetch wrapper that validates Content-Type,\n  checks response.ok, and gives friendly errors for 413/504/non-JSON\n- Rewrite ReferenceUpload: parse references client-side, add size validation\n- Rewrite DocumentUpload: parse document client-side, use safeFetch for\n  style extraction API call\n- Update ProcessingView: use safeFetch with structured retry logic\n- Add pdfjs-dist dependency, remove unused multer\n- Fix next.config.js: add webpack config for pdfjs-dist canvas alias and\n  Node.js polyfill fallbacks for client bundle\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01VangytH8DhEu4NDFFJeduF","tree":{"sha":"94ce0cdec8c8440113238d27ed3106e20f321862","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/git/trees/94ce0cdec8c8440113238d27ed3106e20f321862"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ediakli448/Restyler-Claude/git/commits/1a8c926e2b40ab75fe8d97b03a6fad0ba5eaa6cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 94ce0cdec8c8440113238d27ed3106e20f321862\nparent f137459095259b329c83f4b8caafe709ad1e70a7\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1772973269 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1772973269 +0000\n\nMove document parsing to client-side, fix Vercel 4.5MB payload limit\n\nRoot cause: Uploading PDF/DOCX files as FormData to serverless functions\nhits Vercel''s 4.5MB body size limit, causing 413 errors.\n\nSolution: Parse documents entirely in the browser using pdfjs-dist (PDF)\nand mammoth (DOCX). No file binary ever hits the server — only small\nJSON text payloads are sent to the API routes.\n\nChanges:\n- Add lib/clientParser.js: browser-side PDF/DOCX text + image extraction\n  using pdfjs-dist and mammoth with canvas-based image rendering\n- Add lib/safeFetch.js: robust fetch wrapper that validates Content-Type,\n  checks response.ok, and gives friendly errors for 413/504/non-JSON\n- Rewrite ReferenceUpload: parse references client-side, add size validation\n- Rewrite DocumentUpload: parse document client-side, use safeFetch for\n  style extraction API call\n- Update ProcessingView: use safeFetch with structured retry logic\n- Add pdfjs-dist dependency, remove unused multer\n- Fix next.config.js: add webpack config for pdfjs-dist canvas alias and\n  Node.js polyfill fallbacks for client bundle\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01VangytH8DhEu4NDFFJeduF\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGagSRgR\nrh7lu8rbsQphVf0NBviXfPsY1yVYSsOVM7QaLYOvBsxK/y+rWxwFliIFBMAm3jqgz4k7DbpWeJ9p\ntwY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-08T12:34:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","typ