ions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/b98378301572f473b58d6363842e77443ed94a75/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:23:26Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"rcureton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T16:23:26Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"rcureton"},"message":"feat(tri-lane): 1.10.0 — every task logs itself: worktree lifecycle opens and closes the benchmark record; report.json + verify.jsonl evidence; route declarations; defect windows at session start (Wave 4 T42/T43/T44/T51)\n\nTen days of production (142 tasks) left no benchmark.jsonl because start/end had to be typed and the report was never persisted. Now lane-worktree add / lane-route declare open the record (meta.json), lane-report writes report.json, verify.jsonl and raw verify-<n>.out/.err (timeout keeps partial output and kills the process group; grep/tail/|| pipelines flagged filtered), and lane-worktree remove closes the record from the run dir: route, lane, status, gaps, advisor verdict, rework (spec*.md), dispatches (thread.started), tokens. Labels via --finding; absent = unlabeled. A failed log write never fails a removal. lane-log end --ended-at backfills; due --quiet feeds a fail-open SessionStart hook. codex_logs renamed codex_account (account-wide, never per task). Self-test gains the evidence and record checks; 8 new unit tests (42 total).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/s