ons","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/acf6ada75e98455be6c25ffde7d384203e2333aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T01:57:52Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T01:57:52Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"message":"fix(docs): regenerate OVERVIEW.md after the test-accounts description change\n\nCI caught this, not me: docs/OVERVIEW.md is generated from skill frontmatter and\nfreshness-checked in validate.yml, and editing test-accounts'' `description`\n(6bdd6a0) left it stale. I ran the six gate scripts locally but not the\nregenerate-and-diff step, which exists only as a workflow step.\n\nExactly the generated-artifact drift the repo keeps designing against — and the\ncheck worked.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cqD8v5Ny3L5ezURMeLDag","tree":{"sha":"7d5b9215160a48a6e2758751a649e0eb317ef7ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/trees/7d5b9215160a48a6e2758751a649e0eb317ef7ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/commits/acf6ada75e98455be6c25ffde7d384203e2333aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commit/acf6ada75e98455be6c25ffde7d384203e2333aa","node_id":"C_kwDORh8o4doAKGFjZjZhZGE3NWU5ODQ1NWJlNmMyNWZmZGU3ZDM4NDIwM2UyMzMzYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commit/b7ea465ce5d5ddf158abc6d173656ffd6755d853","sha":"b7ea465ce5d5ddf158abc6d173656ffd6755d853","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/b7ea465ce5d5ddf158abc6d173656ffd6755d853"}],"sha":"acf6ada75e98455be6c25ffde7d384203e2333aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/acf6ada75e98455be6c25ffde7d384203e2333aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/b7ea465ce5d5ddf158abc6d173656ffd6755d853/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T01:55:15Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T01:55:15Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"message":"feat(distribution): translate guardrails into source bodies; retire the .skill pipeline\n\nThe cheap half of Wave 2.5, which the three review passes argued should ship\nwhile T25/T26/T29 wait for a named consumer.\n\nGuardrail translation (the actual exposure). 13 skills gained a READ-ONLY or\nDESTRUCTIVE prose block: 11 whose allowed-tools/disallowed-tools made them\nread-only under Claude Code, and 2 carrying disable-model-invocation. The blocks\nlive in the source SKILL.md so every runtime inherits them.\n\nThis was never an Antigravity problem. Codex ignores Claude-only frontmatter —\nthe same property that let it consume the nested tree unchanged — so the\nmanifests shipped earlier today carry the identical gap. env-secrets-manager is\nthe case that forced it: allowed-tools [Read, Grep, Glob, Bash], disallowed\nWrite/Edit, self-described \"read-only audits\", and it detects secret leaks. On a\nmachine running approval_policy=never and sandbox_mode=danger-full-access it\ninstalls unrestricted. Prose is not enforcement, but it is strictly better than\nsilence and costs hours rather than days.\n\nCI schema coverage. validate.yml now validates .codex-plugin/plugin.json and\n.agents/plugins/marketplace.json, and asserts Codex''s `skills` is a string where\nClaude''s is an array — a wrong type there fails at the consumer''s\n`codex plugin add`, never in CI.\n\nRetired the .skill ZIP pipeline. Deleted gemini skills/ (89 ZIPs) and\ngenerate-gemini-skills.sh, dropped the release step, and scrubbed references\nfrom release.sh, sync-legacy-commands.py, GEMINI.md, CLAUDE.md and\nDISTRIBUTION.md. Confirmed unconsumed first; BACKLOG has said so since July.\n\nCorrects one of my own findings: pass 1 called the reference/ vs references/\nsplit \"a latent bug\". It is not — a link check resolves 50 of 50 relative links\nand both directory names exist where referenced. The earlier check used\nfind -maxdepth 2 and missed directories one level deeper. Cosmetic only, left\nalone rather than churning a dozen files for no consumer.\n\nclaude-commands/ re-synced (14 updated) so the mirror carries the new blocks.\n\nGates: audit, fix-library, sync-metadata, doc-claims, 500-line,\nlegacy-sync, skill-scripts — all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cqD8v5Ny3L5ezURMeLDag","tree":{"sha":"bd3b136e130e1dcc9f70ae6b967b24c5213288f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/trees/bd3b136e130e1dcc9f70ae6b967b24c5213288f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/commits/b7ea465ce5d5ddf158abc6d173656ffd6755d853","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commit/b7ea465ce5d5ddf158abc6d173656ffd6755d853","node_id":"C_kwDORh8o4doAKGI3ZWE0NjVjZTVkNWRkZjE1OGFiYzZkMTczNjU2ZmZkNjc1NWQ4NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commit/d22bd493723073df27e0e6183ac86a9a51e4b260","sha":"d22bd493723073df27e0e6183ac86a9a51e4b260","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/d22bd493723073df27e0e6183ac86a9a51e4b260"}],"sha":"b7ea465ce5d5ddf158abc6d173656ffd6755d853","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/b7ea465ce5d5ddf158abc6d173656ffd6755d853"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/d22bd493723073df27e0e6183ac86a9a51e4b260/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T00:57:46Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T00:57:46Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"message":"docs(backlog): three adversarial re-scope passes on Wave 2.5; recommend descoping\n\nThree passes over T25/T26/T29, each measured against the tree rather than\nreasoned from the tickets. Conclusion is not \"do A\".\n\nPass 1 (counts): the exporter copies too little — bodies link to reference/,\nreferences/, workflows/ and assets/ (~50 links) that would 404; dist/ would be\nthe third generated mirror after claude-commands/; the destination namespace\nis shared with 17 foreign skills and nothing guards collisions.\n\nPass 2 (behaviour and security): T25.3 translates disallowed-tools and\ndisable-model-invocation but ignores allowed-tools, which 16 skills set and 8\nuse to stay read-only — so as written it warns on 6 skills and silently widens\n16. docs/ alone is referenced by 35 skills, making this a link-rewriting\nproblem T25 budgets nothing for. context: fork (17) and paths: (4) are\nstripped with nothing in their place.\n\nPass 3 (premise, including work already merged): the wave exists to give\ncredit-exhausted consultants a fallback runtime, but Codex now serves that\nwith no export at all, and Antigravity''s only in-org use — the tri-lane review\nlane — passes a self-contained spec and never invokes library skills. Meanwhile\nthe guardrail gap found in pass 2 applies verbatim to Codex, which shipped\ntoday: env-secrets-manager is read-only under Claude and unrestricted there,\non a machine set to approval_policy=never and sandbox_mode=danger-full-access.\nThat is the highest-priority item here and it belongs to merged work, not to A.\n\nRecommends shipping the cheap half (guardrail translation into source bodies,\nCI schema coverage for the Codex manifests, retiring the dead ZIP pipeline,\nfixing reference/ vs references/) and deferring T25/T26/T29 until a named\nconsumer exists. Also withdraws pass 1''s suggestion to fold claude-commands/\ninto the exporter as scope creep, and replaces \"re-probe the paths\" with a\nfalsifiable experiment that carries a positive control.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cqD8v5Ny3L5ezURMeLDag","tree":{"sha":"925d84674c07ac0147bbb8fe85e7aaadd9c2b8f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/trees/925d84674c07ac0147bbb8fe85e7aaadd9c2b8f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/commits/d22bd493723073df27e0e6183ac86a9a51e4b260","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commit/d22bd493723073df27e0e6183ac86a9a51e4b260","node_id":"C_kwDORh8o4doAKGQyMmJkNDkzNzIzMDczZGYyN2UwZTYxODNhYzg2YTlhNTFlNGIyNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commit/3b97098af701c960d1e76c2a2451f3d73b185468","sha":"3b97098af701c960d1e76c2a2451f3d73b185468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/3b97098af701c960d1e76c2a2451f3d73b185468"}],"sha":"d22bd493723073df27e0e6183ac86a9a51e4b260","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/d22bd493723073df27e0e6183ac86a9a51e4b260"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/3b97098af701c960d1e76c2a2451f3d73b185468/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T00:36:51Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T00:36:51Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"message":"docs(backlog): amend Wave 2.5 with probed vendor behaviour and revised sequencing\n\nT25/T26/T29 were scoped from documentation in July 2026. Probing the real\nCLIs (codex-cli 0.153.4, agy 1.1.27) contradicts three of their assumptions,\nso this records what was measured and what changes, without rewriting the\nticket text.\n\n- T26 hangs freshness on auto-update.sh, which is dead: PLUGIN_DIR resolves\n  to a dangling symlink into a deleted sprint0 node_modules vendoring, so it\n  exits 1 before doing anything. Replaced with a three-layer model (CI\n  regenerate-and-diff, a source-SHA check at the install root, and an agy\n  lane preflight gate).\n- T26''s \"universal workspace path\" claim did not hold: neither\n  .agents/skills/ nor .agents/skills.json loaded at agy 1.1.27, though both\n  are documented inside the binary. Only ~/.gemini/config/skills/ is\n  confirmed. Flagged for re-probe before T26 is built.\n- Codex needs no export at all — it reads the nested tree directly as of\n  today''s manifests, so the exporter is Gemini/Antigravity-only.\n- T25 item 5 (duplicate-name failure) is now enforced upstream by\n  audit-library.py, so the exporter''s check becomes a second line of defence.\n\nAdds a step 0 re-probe that gates the rest, and keeps retiring the .skill ZIP\npipeline as a separate final change so it stays revertible on its own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cqD8v5Ny3L5ezURMeLDag","tree":{"sha":"46e69264a9eb6fc7b3a46cc7a96e9b3a0084dde6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/trees/46e69264a9eb6fc7b3a46cc7a96e9b3a0084dde6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/commits/3b97098af701c960d1e76c2a2451f3d73b185468","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commit/3b97098af701c960d1e76c2a2451f3d73b185468","node_id":"C_kwDORh8o4doAKDNiOTcwOThhZjcwMWM5NjBkMWU3NmMyYTI0NTFmM2Q3M2IxODU0Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commit/6bdd6a0f5cc370dce8e1e8e172ceccb91356c0bd","sha":"6bdd6a0f5cc370dce8e1e8e172ceccb91356c0bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/6bdd6a0f5cc370dce8e1e8e172ceccb91356c0bd"}],"sha":"3b97098af701c960d1e76c2a2451f3d73b185468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/3b97098af701c960d1e76c2a2451f3d73b185468"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/6bdd6a0f5cc370dce8e1e8e172ceccb91356c0bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T00:35:18Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T00:35:18Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"message":"feat(test-accounts): QA email provisioning, addressing strategy, cascading teardown\n\nThe skill covered personas, seeders and compliance fixtures but had zero\ncoverage of the addresses those personas actually receive mail on — no\nplus-addressing, catch-all, inbox-API or teardown guidance anywhere in it.\n\nAdds an \"Email Address Strategy\" section before Step 3 (personas inherit the\nchoice) plus reference/email-accounts.md with the address generator, E2E\ninbox polling, and a cascading teardown script.\n\nPosition taken deliberately: do NOT standardize on plus-addressing. It is\nreal (RFC 5233) but forms reject \"+\", apps that normalize email collide every\nvariant into one account, and every reset link lands in one human''s inbox —\nwhich makes that inbox a credential. Default is a catch-all on a dedicated\nnon-production domain, with a programmatic inbox API for CI, since reading a\nverification code back into a test is the thing plus-addressing cannot do.\n\nTeardown is the part that leaks: one account is a row in five systems, and\ndeleting only the auth user orphans the Stripe customer, which costs money on\na metered plan. Deletion is gated on both the existing environment guard and\na positive isQaEmail() allow-list.\n\nReaping is on-demand (npm run qa:reap), never scheduled — Cure org policy\nsince 2026-08-08 forbids cron jobs, which rules out the nightly-cleanup\ndesign every external example assumes.\n\nSection is unnumbered so the existing reference links to \"Step 4\" and\n\"Step 8\" keep resolving.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019cqD8v5Ny3L5ezURMeLDag","tree":{"sha":"1dfb5f1de7a5760e23d5d5e598f21bc155eddc0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/trees/1dfb5f1de7a5760e23d5d5e598f21bc155eddc0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/commits/6bdd6a0f5cc370dce8e1e8e172ceccb91356c0bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Cure-Consult