75dc479300c1585dec14a1ba2"}],"sha":"7892137a1bb38e2871b9a014c600b76db1bbd074","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/7892137a1bb38e2871b9a014c600b76db1bbd074"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16387538?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Rcureton","id":16387538,"login":"Rcureton","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2Mzg3NTM4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rcureton","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/commits/f45496eb88aa63d75dc479300c1585dec14a1ba2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T16:56:51Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T16:56:51Z","email":"rashad.cureton@gmail.com","name":"Rashad Cureton"},"message":"feat(design-studio): expand into a full multidisciplinary design studio\n\nCapability audit against the studio brief (design intelligence, register\nchoice, platform specialisation, scrolling and states, wireframing, UX\narchitecture, brand identity, design systems, cross-platform, responsive,\naccessibility, typography, motion, asset production, mobile assets,\ndata-dense design, content-aware design, three-perspective review, critique,\nanti-patterns, deliverable scaling, visual output, decision records,\nimplementation awareness, quality bar).\n\nSKILL.md is now the router (classify -> context -> architecture -> concept ->\nplatforms -> systemise -> produce -> panel -> critique -> deliver); judgment\nlives in nine sibling references (design-intelligence, ux-architecture,\nplatform-apple/android/web, design-system-spec, brand-identity,\ndesign-review-panel, critique-and-quality-bar).\n\nNew stdlib tools: wireframe.py (device-framed lo/mid-fi wireframes with\nfixed/sticky/scroll regions, flow diagram, inventory with the scroll model),\ncontrast_check.py (WCAG pairs by token convention, per light/dark mode),\ntokens_lint.py (three tiers, naming, aliases, mode parity),\ndesign_review_panel.py (Creative / UX / Systems director prompts; --run on\nclaude, codex, gemini CLIs). export_asset_matrix.py rewritten around a\nrenderer chain (rsvg-convert, Inkscape, ImageMagick, Chrome headless,\nQuick Look) with pixel-level transparency verification and iOS / Android\nicon sets; figma_sync.py resolves aliases and publishes light/dark modes.\nStarter token schema restructured into the three tiers.\n\nTested on two representative assignments (recruiting app for iOS + web;\nfintech brand identity); defects they surfaced are fixed here: Quick Look\nflattening alpha to white, squashed feature graphic, contrast pairing that\ncontradicted the token naming convention, wireframe example leaking the\neval answer, review panel drowning in SVG bodies, missing brief step.\n\nevals: t20-product-ux-architecture added under design-studio.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DwSxJmkV1JbhmK5LBHPE5f","tree":{"sha":"e4255f414f182d584c15eab3628cbfb324dc2653","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringSkills/git/trees/e4255f414f182d584c15eab3628cbfb324dc2653"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Cure-Consulting-Group/ProductEngineeringS