","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus49/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus49/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus49/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nexus49","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ifdotpy/marketplace-ui-detached-archive/commits/dc57c94176faec4fc035edc320f4825a29c6bf86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-08-06T06:17:43Z","email":"bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com","name":"Bastian Echterhölter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-06T06:17:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: adding detail view and installation (#7)\n\n* feat(package): update start script to include serve path\n\n- Modified the start script in package.json to set the serve path for the Angular application.\n- Ensures the application serves from the specified path for the marketplace UI.\n\n* feat(graphql): add initial GraphQL schema and configuration\n\n- Introduced graphql.config.yml for schema and document paths\n- Created schema.graphql with core queries and mutations\n- Defined types for DeleteOptions, Status, and MarketplaceEntry\n- Implemented input types for mutations and queries\n\n* feat(graphql): enhance marketplace entry retrieval\n\n- Refactored getMarketplaceEntry to utilize Apollo client for querying marketplace entries.\n- Removed unused parameters and commented-out code for clarity.\n- Improved filtering logic to return the correct marketplace entry based on provider name.\n- Updated error handling in provider metadata effects for better resilience.\n\n* feat: remove mocks\n\n* feat(graphql): enhance provider installation process\n\n- Added metadata field to the API export specification.\n- Updated InstallProviderInput to use MarketplaceEntry instead of providerInput and displayName.\n- Refactored installProviderInstance method to simplify input handling.\n- Introduced createAPIBindingMutation for creating API bindings in GraphQL.\n- Enhanced GraphqlService to utilize the new mutation for provider installation.","tree":{"sha":"5088e5dbd820acceb480b1fc1fda1aa0dc79f99c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ifdotpy/marketplace-ui-detached-archive/git/trees/5088e5dbd820acceb480b1fc1fda1aa0dc79f99c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ifdotpy/marketplace-ui-detached-archive/git/commits/dc57c94176faec4fc035edc320f4825a29c6bf86","verification":{"payload":"tree 5088e5dbd820acceb480b1fc1fda1aa0dc79f99c\nparent e64cd46a8972f59d96f86bc4383438ee5168290f\nauthor Bastian Echterhölter <bastian.echterhoelter@sap.com> 1754461063 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1754461063 +0200\n\nfeat: adding detail view and installation (#7)\n\n* feat(package): update start script to include serve path\n\n- Modified the start script in package.json to set the serve path for the Angular application.\n- Ensures the application serves from the specified path for the marketplace UI.\n\n* feat(graphql): add initial GraphQL schema and configuration\n\n- Introduced graphql.config.yml for schema and document paths\n- Created schema.graphql with core queries and mutations\n- Defined types for DeleteOptions, Status, and MarketplaceEntry\n- Implemented input types for mutations and queries\n\n* feat(graphql): enhance marketplace entry retrieval\n\n- Refactored getMarketplaceEntry to utilize Apollo client for querying marketplace entries.\n- Removed unused parameters and commented-out code for clarity.\n- Improved filtering logic to return the correct marketplace entry based on provider name.\n- Updated error handling in provider metadata effects for better resilience.\n\n* feat: remove mocks\n\n* feat(graphql): enhance provider installation process\n\n- Added metadata field to the API export specification.\n- Updated InstallProviderInput to use MarketplaceEntry instead of providerInput and displayName.\n- Refactored installProviderInstance method to simplify